    "explanation": "To Driver D-37932 and Rider R-94198: this no-show cannot be decided on the record, so the case goes to a human reviewer and the SGD 5.00 already refunded to the rider is held, not collected or paid out.\n\nWhat the record settles. EV-TRIP-05064 shows the driver marked arrival at 15:42:00, and on an on-demand booking (no scheduled time) the POL-NS-21 free wait runs from that marker, expiring at 15:47:05, with the cancellation as a rider no-show at 15:49:00. The POL-NS-23 contact obligation is met: two in-app messages (15:42:20, 15:46:00) and one in-app call (15:45:10) all precede the 15:49:00 cancellation, so nothing is voided under that clause. EV-FARE-05064 shows a single cancellation fee of 5.00 SGD, exactly the policy fee, so POL-NS-22's fee-amount check raises no referral; no other referral clause fires (the rider's profile carries no repeat no-show counter under POL-NS-25, and POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not apply because the driver did attempt contact).\n\nWhat is not settled, and why it decides the case. POL-NS-21's free wait runs from the driver's arrival, and the policy's arrival test treats the driver as at the pickup only where the trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace within 50 m. The only GPS trace, EV-GPS-05064, is impaired at weight 0.6 with issue code GPS_GAP_STRADDLING_CANCELLATION: one 720-second hole from 15:38:00 to 15:50:00 that swallows the arrival marker, the whole waiting window and the cancellation, with the nearest fixes several hundred metres from Block 33 and the trace's own arrival check returning no corroborating fix. That is precisely the stretch the arrival test reads, so the arrival is undecided — neither corroborated nor disproved. The arrival marker is a status the driver set; the platform events that follow (rider notified 15:42:04, wait timer 15:42:05) are triggered by it and do not independently place the car at the kerb.\n\nOn the driver's claims: I accept the free-wait arithmetic (POL-NS-21), the contact obligation (POL-NS-23), the 5.00 SGD amount (EV-FARE-05064), and that POL-NS-24 gives the rider no refund route — but the free wait's start depends on an arrival the record cannot establish, so the fee cannot be transferred to the driver under POL-NS-22 and the DRIVER_COMPENSATION and POL-GEN-03 arguments built on it fail for that reason. I reject the submission that no deciding fact is impaired: the deciding fact — whether the driver was at the pickup — is carried only by the impaired trace, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 0.6, not 1.0.\n\nOn the rider's claims: I accept that the arrival is uncorroborated, that the driver's own message 'I'm at Blk 33 pick-up point' does not cure it, that POL-NS-23 compliance does not substitute for the arrival, and that POL-GEN-26 requires escalation. I do not accept that this yields NO_ACTION. NO_ACTION would leave the rider's refund in place, which is effectively to hold the fee void; no clause voids it (the driver did contact, and the rider did not cancel), and reading voidance off the missing corroboration is exactly the inference from absence that POL-GEN-26 forbids. For the same reason POL-GEN-03 does not direct DRIVER_COMPENSATION: the driver is owed the 5.00 SGD back only if the fee stands, and that is undecided. The rider's account that he was at the pickup and never saw the car is noted, but no clause makes a counterparty statement the test for the arrival, so it cannot decide that limb either way.\n\nOutcome: the 5.00 SGD moved by the 2026-09-06 19:30 fee_reversed event is held pending review. Open question for the reviewer: was the driver at Block 33, Jalan Bukit Merah during the free-wait window 15:42:00–15:47:00 on 2026-09-06? Confidence is 0.6, capped by the 0.6 weight of the impaired GPS trace that carries the undecided fact."
  },
